      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry I wasn\u0027t a part of that discussion. I see Keith mentioning the same thing about the enum-name. Though I think that the initialization can still be done there and gets rid of duplication of logic. Basically if I want to move a GPIO from used to unused I would imagine it should be as simple as just removing the enum-name (same applies for the inverse). As for the logic, we don\u0027t need to do this in the same loop, couldn\u0027t we set the GPIO to `(GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_PULL_UP)` in something like:\n\n#define GPIO_UNINIT(inst) \\\n  gpio_pin_configure(get_device_binding(inst), DT_GPIO_PIN(inst, gpios), \\\n                     CONFIG_GPIO_UNINIT_FLAGS);\n\n#define GPIO_UNINIT_COND(inst) \\\n  COND_CODE_0(DT_NODE_HAS_PROP(id, enum_name), (GPIO_UNINIT(id), ), ())\n\nstatic some_init_function(const struct device *unused) {\n#if DT_NODE_EXISTS(DT_PATH(named_gpios))\n  DT_FOREACH_CHILD(DT_PATH(named_gpios), GPIO_UNINIT_COND)\n#endif\n}\nSYS_INIT(...)",
